## 2026-08-14

- Implemented the complete CDECR MU300 narrow wall-time remediation without running real-model acceptance: provider/transport failures no longer trigger content repair; Package V3 clustering remains high reasoning while description uses independently versioned low reasoning; description checkpoints, Registry finalize, and V3 activation use batched/preloaded persistence under the existing atomic CAS boundary; Field task state is coordinator-batched and semantic query embeddings are prewarmed and cached by exact raw-text hash; embedding batches use a provider-aware 8/4 safety policy and do not recursively split timeout/402/429/transport failures; persisted Atomic cosine recall uses deterministic float64 matrix multiplication with scalar boundary checks; and BULK read paths use query-only WAL snapshot connections while writers retain the serialized transaction gate. Added rollback settings, focused deterministic tests, and connection/batch telemetry; no external provider call, frozen replay, 30-document acceptance, or MU300 run was performed.
- Added one shared time-awareness guard to generated Codex D1 Pilot task prompts: every node now receives the current U.S. Eastern date in `EST YYYY-MM-DD` form plus a concise requirement that all report content and conclusions remain useful at that date. The date is computed at case-generation time through `America/New_York`, without duplicating instructions across node agents or skills.

## 2026-08-12

- Fixed the Codex D1 v2 C1 Pilot prompt injection regression: replaced the 377-byte placeholder fundamental skill and abbreviated agent prompt with the complete governed C1 prompt/skill, aligned the attempt contract to the six required C1 report sections, and added a parity regression test against the canonical internal skill. Added a C1-only `quality` Pilot profile that removes inherited functional-smoke brevity constraints and makes formal research the primary task while retaining bounded blocker/major Pilot logging.

- Extended persistent research-quality Pilot generation to C3, O4-A, and all three C4 turns. Attempt bundles now inject canonical governed agents/skills instead of the abbreviated asset copies, C3/O4-A use their complete six-section contracts, O4-A has a dedicated second-turn prompt, and C4 receives a structured five-field task contract rather than nonexistent progressive Markdown instructions. Hardened Pilot Doctor to reject failed semantic envelopes and assigned a valid SEC probe to C4; generated and verified independent NVDA quality cases for C3, O4-A, C4 pre-scan, enrichment, and finalization.

- Fixed two C4 App Pilot blockers found in the first pre-scan attempt: non-progressive attempt bundles now declare and seed a unique writable `structured_output_path`, and generated Pilot tasks hard-check that the Codex project root is the exact case directory before MCP preflight. This prevents a parent-directory launch from silently skipping the case-local `.codex/config.toml` and being misdiagnosed as a capability failure. Bumped the attempt task contract to v3 and included that version in stable input hashing so the corrected task cannot share a misleading SHA with the broken contract.

- Hardened Pilot case regeneration against Data MCP catalog drift: the builder now removes only the selected current attempt's exported catalog before making the case read-only, allowing the current governed tool contract to regenerate it while preserving upstream catalogs and the attempt Observation Store.

